WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:18.091
"Are you ready for battle, my boys?" shouted Peter with great excitement.

2
00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:27.478
From various parts of the lagoon, the boys answered, "Ay, ay! We'll get those pirates!"

3
00:00:27.479 --> 00:00:30.265
And the battle was on.

4
00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:37.481
The boys fought bravely against Smee and Starkey, forcing them out of their boat and into the water.

5
00:00:37.482 --> 00:00:42.370
Heads bobbed up and down. It was a close fight.

6
00:00:42.371 --> 00:00:48.521
At last, the boys captured the boat, and the two pirates swam away.

7
00:00:48.522 --> 00:00:55.239
Fearless as they were, none of the boys wanted to fight Captain Hook, who was in the water too.

8
00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:02.916
They had promised Peter that Captain Hook would be his, but they also trembled at the thought of Hook's iron claw.

9
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:10.790
It was at this battle, on Marooners' Rock, that Peter and Hook would finally meet face-to-face!

10
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:14.352
Hook pulled himself up on the rock to take a breath.

11
00:01:14.353 --> 00:01:17.171
Peter climbed up the other side.

12
00:01:17.172 --> 00:01:23.089
Because the rock was slippery, they had to crawl on their knees, keeping their heads down.

13
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.533
Neither knew the other was coming.

14
00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:31.613
As they both reached for a grip on the slippery rock, their hands suddenly touched.

15
00:01:31.614 --> 00:01:36.765
Their heads popped up, and Hook and Peter were nose to nose.

16
00:01:36.766 --> 00:01:40.793
Quickly, Peter grabbed the knife from Hook's belt.

17
00:01:40.794 --> 00:01:46.414
But before he struck his foe, Peter noticed that he was on the highest part of the rock.

18
00:01:46.415 --> 00:01:49.273
It seemed very unfair.

19
00:01:49.274 --> 00:01:58.021
So instead of stabbing Hook right away, Peter extended his hand to help Hook up so they would both be on equal footing.

20
00:01:58.022 --> 00:02:02.358
But rather than taking Peter's hand, Hook bit it.

21
00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:07.327
Outraged, Peter stood motionless. He was in shock.

22
00:02:07.328 --> 00:02:11.026
People remember the first time life is unfair to them.

23
00:02:11.027 --> 00:02:16.564
Though they may forgive the unfairness, they are never quite the same after.

24
00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:22.390
But not Peter. He had met unfairness before, but he always forgot.

25
00:02:22.391 --> 00:02:28.149
Perhaps this was the real difference between Peter and other boys who grow older.

26
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:33.600
While Peter stood there stunned, Hook's iron hand clawed him several times.

27
00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.267
Peter was badly wounded.

28
00:02:36.268 --> 00:02:41.008
During the battle, the Lost Boys lost track of Wendy and Peter.

29
00:02:41.009 --> 00:02:46.958
After a while they saw Hook in the water swimming away as fast as he could.

30
00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:51.825
Behind him was the crocodile in pursuit of his favorite food.

31
00:02:51.826 --> 00:02:55.647
The boys decided to make their way back home.

32
00:02:55.648 --> 00:03:03.405
Occasionally they shouted "Peter! Wendy!" but they expected no answer.

33
00:03:03.406 --> 00:03:08.513
They were sure that Peter and Wendy had already made it back home.

34
00:03:08.514 --> 00:03:14.570
Left behind, Wendy had swum around the lagoon on her own and was now worn-out.

35
00:03:14.571 --> 00:03:19.333
With his last bit of strength, Peter pulled her up onto Marooners' Rock.

36
00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:24.866
They both lay there, tired and weak and unable to speak.

37
00:03:24.867 --> 00:03:32.561
The tide was coming in. Finally Peter said, "Look, the water is rising."

38
00:03:32.562 --> 00:03:36.874
Wendy did not understand, so Peter tried to explain.

39
00:03:36.875 --> 00:03:42.011
"You're too weak to swim or fly home, and I am badly wounded.

40
00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:44.897
Soon the water will cover this rock."

41
00:03:44.898 --> 00:03:50.152
"You mean we are going to drown?" she asked weakly.

42
00:03:50.153 --> 00:03:55.218
"Unless we find a way to leave this rock," he answered.

43
00:03:55.219 --> 00:04:01.707
As they clung to each other, Peter searched the water for something that might keep them afloat.

44
00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:06.055
Floating by was Starkey's hat. Quickly, Peter grabbed it.

45
00:04:06.056 --> 00:04:09.123
But it was too small to be of much help.

46
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:12.816
Nevertheless, he placed it on his head.

47
00:04:12.817 --> 00:04:17.594
Then suddenly something very light brushed against Peter.

48
00:04:17.595 --> 00:04:20.998
It was the tail of a kite that was flying high above.

49
00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:26.074
Michael had made it some days ago, and it had blown away.

50
00:04:26.075 --> 00:04:29.693
"Look it's Michael's kite!" said Peter.

51
00:04:29.694 --> 00:04:34.502
"It might be able to carry you home." Peter grabbed hold of it.

52
00:04:34.503 --> 00:04:39.162
With new energy, he tied the string of the kite around Wendy's waist.

53
00:04:39.163 --> 00:04:45.541
"What about you?" asked Wendy. "You must tie it around yourself too."

54
00:04:45.542 --> 00:04:51.712
"This kite isn't big enough. It will only lift one person," replied Peter.

55
00:04:51.713 --> 00:04:55.529
"I won't go without you," said Wendy.

56
00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:00.949
But, with his last bit of strength, Peter had already pushed her from the rock.

57
00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:09.441
In seconds, she was in the air and almost out of sight.
